mod:pointer_back_into_holder;
// 2026-11-13 (landing 177d2b6, row 2: DEF-663 and DEF-665, A+B). A POINTER MEMBER THAT POINTS BACK INTO ITS OWN HOLDER, OR INTO THE HOLDER IT WAS REACHED FROM,
// IS FOLLOWED TO WHAT IT POINTS AT. `targets_held` and `pointer_targets_of`'s two loops skipped a ref rooted at the holder itself, or at the holder the walk came
// from, before the target test, so `s.p = @s.own` or `s.back = @q.own` added nothing to what the pointer reaches: a `List` grown through the pointer while a
// pointer into the member was held, then that pointer read, read freed heap (DEF-663). `check_pointer_view_parties` skipped a view party rooted at the write's
// own root, so a view or a pointer taken through `s.p` into `s.own` was never checked against a write of `s.own` by name (DEF-665). A+B tests such a ref as a
// target at all three sites and skips it only for the hop, and drops the view side's skip, so the party is re-rooted at the pointer's target by the loop below it.
// One cell a face, its names suffixed with the cell's. Each face is accepted by row 1 (23eba2f), main (8a2b40b), 169d6d4 and b510126 (177d2b3), and reads
// freed memory there (236 at -O0 and -O2 on roads 0 to 2, or 140 for the two string views below, and 97 under the detector). Each face's right control is
// in `pointer_back_into_holder_ok.npk`, but `c2_backv`'s and `c2_backpl`'s, which the cells don't have. The row closes 19 faces and refuses no right program.
// DEF-663's nine (Ailp-team_114's attack on 177d2b5's row 5; management_41's ruling of Thu 11-12 15:42:18 EST and management_42's of 15:53:31 and 16:08:01):
// `c1_back`, `c2_backt`, `c2_backpl` (`s.back = @q.own`, `q` the holder `s` was reached from, handed back by a getter), `c2_backv` (the view through the getter's
// pointer, the growth by name), `c2_self` (`s.inn.p = @s.own`, handed back by a getter), `c10_nmself`, `c10_inself` (`s.p = @s.own`, grown through `s.p` or
// `bp.p`, one frame, no getter), `c11_selfw2` (pushed through `@s.p.l` inline) and `c13_selfar` (`s.p = @s.ar[0i64]`): BORROW-015 at the growth.
// DEF-665's `c11_selfv`: `int64->:e = @((<-(s.p)).l[0i64]);`, then `s.own.l` pushed by name: BORROW-015 at the push.
// The seven boundary forms (Ailp-team_120, 177d2b6's planning): `d1_lst` (a `List<int64>->` member into a `List` member), `d3_inn` (a nested struct's pointer),
// `d4_arr` (an array of holders, one element's pointer into its sibling), BORROW-015 at the growth; `v1_inn`, `v3_arr` (the same two through the view side),
// `v4_whole` (`s.own = …` by name) and `v5_call` (`growh(@s.own)`), BORROW-015 at the write.
// DEF-665's view form (this row's, nitpick-compiler_120: its mutant that restored the skip for a view party alone survived the 17 above): `vw_self`, with
// `s.p = @s.own`, holds `fixed uint8[]:vw = string_bytes((<-(s.p)).s);` and assigns `s.own.s` by name, and `vw_selfw` assigns `s.own` whole: BORROW-015 at
// the write.
// DEF-418'S OPEN FACES BESIDE THESE, NOT CLOSED BY THIS ROW (F on every build; management_42's ruling of Fri 11-13 02:57:34 EST: "the two roots can be one
// argument and a pointer member of its pointee"): `d5_ptrp` and `v6_ptrp`, the holder handed by pointer to a callee (`h(@s)`) that holds `@sp.own.l[0i64]` and
// grows through `sp.p`, or holds `@((<-(sp.p)).l[0i64])` and pushes `@sp.own.l`. Named here; an accepted cell has no site.
error:E5;
struct:K_c1_back = { int64:k; };
func:mk_c1_back = List<int64>() never fails { List<int64>:l = raw list_init::<int64>(2i64); drop list_push(@l, 1i64); drop list_push(@l, 2i64); pass l; };
struct:HL_c1_back = { List<int64>:l; int64:k; };
func:mkh_c1_back = HL_c1_back() never fails { pass HL_c1_back{ l: raw mk_c1_back(), k: 1i64 }; };
func:growh_c1_back = int64(HL_c1_back->:w) never fails { loop(0i64, 64i64, 1i64) { drop list_push(@w.l, 1i64); } pass 7i64; };
struct:S_c1_back = { HL_c1_back->:back; int64:z; };
struct:Sub_c1_back = { S_c1_back->:sp; int64:z; };
struct:Q_c1_back = { Sub_c1_back:sub; HL_c1_back:own; };
func:get_c1_back = HL_c1_back->(Sub_c1_back->:sb) never fails { pass (<-(sb.sp)).back; };
func:g_c1_back = int64(int64:n) never fails {
    HL_c1_back:d = raw mkh_c1_back();
    S_c1_back:s = S_c1_back{ back: @d, z: 1i64 };
    Q_c1_back:q = Q_c1_back{ sub: Sub_c1_back{ sp: @s, z: 1i64 }, own: raw mkh_c1_back() };
    s.back = @q.own;
    HL_c1_back->:hp = raw get_c1_back(@q.sub);
    int64->:e = @q.own.l[0i64];
    discard(raw growh_c1_back(hp));
    pass (<-e) + 6i64;
};
